The first statement initializes `type` to `curr_type` only if `type` is -1, which means that if no MTRR covers the GFN, `type` remains -1. The second statement issues a warning if there is a partial mapping, which can occur when the function encounters GFNs not covered by any MTRRs, leading to excessive warnings during device assignment.

